<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nova Reforma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as New Reform</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nova Reforma, or New Reform, was a reform of the institutions of Andorra approved by its co-princes in 1866 and led by the syndic Guillem d'Areny-Plandolit. It replaced the narrow oligarchic system of government with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-council-of-andorra">Consell General</a> elected by the heads of household of each parish, widening political participation while keeping the medieval co-principality intact. It remained the basis of Andorran government until the twentieth century.</p></div>
